"""Walk-through of lesson 27, Observability.

Example numbers (mine, checked by script): 100 checkouts a second; SLO "99.9% of checkouts succeed in under 1 second" leaves an error budget of 0.1%:
100 x 30 x 24 x 3600 = 259,200,000 checkouts in 30 days, so 259,200 failures are allowed. 5% errors = burn rate 50 = budget gone in 14.4 h; 6% = 60 = 12 h.
Trace: checkout 1,000 ms = 20 own + 80 payments + 900 inventory; inventory 900 = 20 own + one 880 ms query (88% of the checkout). After an index (5 ms): 20 + 80 + 20 + 5 = 125 ms.
Incident: release at 03:04, errors 0.1% -> 6% at 03:12, rollback at 03:19: 7 min x 60 s x 100/s x 6% = 2,520 failed checkouts = 0.97% of the monthly budget.
"""
